  ═══ NO VISIBLE FAQ IS RENDERED HERE — DELIBERATE, 2026-08-23 ═══

  A metafield-driven visible FAQ block was added here and REMOVED the same day.
  Recording why, so it is not re-added:

  The 2026-08-23 audit listed these three pages as having "no FAQ":
      /pages/vetements-second-hand-maroc
      /pages/second-hand-clothing-morocco
      /pages/second-hand-clothing-marrakech
  That reading was wrong. It measured FAQPage *schema*, and all three already
  carry 4-5 visible <details> Q&A written into the page BODY. Rendering a second
  list from the metafield printed the same topics twice on every one of them.

  The real gap was schema-only. It is fixed by populating page.metafields.lbass.faq
  to MIRROR the questions already visible in the body — snippets/lbass-page-faq-schema.liquid
  then emits FAQPage from it, and nothing new is drawn on the page.

  THE RULE: the metafield describes what the body already shows. If you edit the
  visible Q&A in a page body, edit the metafield to match — FAQPage that
  describes questions a visitor cannot see is a structured-data violation.
{%- endcomment -%}

